{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:21:41.218Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 2. Summary of what was done:\n\n**Implementation**\n- **`src/core/vcs/land-stop.ts`** (new): `recordLandStop(config, change, stop)` writes the `.run/regressed/change.md` marker and the `regressed` event line (matching `haltWorktreeChange`'s shape), then commits both on the change's branch as `osq: <id> land stopped` authored by `vcs.author`. On commit failure it resets the paths, restores the prior file contents, and throws `osq could not record the stop: <git output>`. Exports `recordsLandStop(reason)`.\n- **`src/core/vcs/land.ts`**: catches `SyncStop` from `syncWithDefaultBranch`; records `sync_conflict`, `requirement_changed`, and `sync_verify_red` stops and rethrows the sync message (or message + failed-commit line); other errors rethrow unchanged. 241 lines.\n- **`src/core/vcs/land-checks.ts`**: new `assertNoSteering(change)` derives state in the change's own tree and refuses with `<folder> needs steering: <describeTrigger>; run osq plan <id>`. Called after the worktree-clean check and before `assertNoEarlierChange`, only for not-landed changes.\n- **`tests/vcs-land-steering.test.ts`** (new): four scenarios covering conflict recording, red-verify recording, non-trigger stops recording nothing, and the next land refusing until steered.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/vcs-land-steering.test.ts`: 4/4 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: exit 0 (typechecks, UI typecheck, build, 2898 + 94 tests, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/.run/results/2.md`."}}
